# .env.example
# ===========================================================================
# Jira, Confluence, and GitHub are reached through their MCP servers
# (jira-epam, Atlassian, and GitHub MCP, declared in .vscode/mcp.json), which
# carry their own credentials (VS Code prompts for the Jira and GitHub tokens
# on first start). With those servers started in your editor, you should not
# need provider tokens here.
#
# This file lists the only environment values the pipeline might read, for the
# rare case a skill runs in raw-API fallback instead of via an MCP server.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you need. `.env` is git-ignored and is
# never read into agent context or committed.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Jira (fallback only; prefer the Atlassian MCP server) ---
# JIRA_BASE_URL=https://jiraeu.epam.com/
# JIRA_EMAIL=you@example.com
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=<your-jira-api-token>
# JIRA_PROJECT_KEY=EPMCDMETST

# --- Confluence (fallback only; prefer the Atlassian MCP server) ---
# CONFLUENCE_BASE_URL=https://your-company.atlassian.net/
# CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN=<your-confluence-api-token>
# CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY=TaskLite

# --- GitHub (fallback only; prefer the GitHub MCP server) ---
# GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-token>
# GITHUB_REPO=https://github.com/cprash/tasklite-ai-sdlc-github-copilot
# GITHUB_BASE_BRANCH=main
